The Linux AppImage includes libmpv 0.41 (https://mpv.io) with FFmpeg,
libplacebo, libass, dav1d and the other libraries linked into it, as built
by https://github.com/jason-yau/mpv-prebuilt (GPL build, release named in
usr/share/doc/libmpv/manifest.txt). mpv in this build is licensed under the
GNU General Public License version 2 or later; the licenses of everything
it contains are in usr/share/doc/libmpv/licenses.

The Android APK includes CPython (https://www.python.org), from the Android
binary release python.org publishes for each Python version
(python-<version>-<host>.tar.gz for arm64-v8a and x86_64; the version is
PYTHON_ANDROID_VERSION in .github/pins.env), under the Python Software
Foundation License Version 2. It is built with OpenSSL (Apache License 2.0),
SQLite (public domain), libffi (MIT), xz/liblzma (public domain), bzip2
(BSD-style) and zstd (BSD-3-Clause or GPL-2.0, taken under BSD-3-Clause); it
contains no GNU readline or gdbm. Its small launcher
(android/packaging/python-launcher.c) is Lumtub's. The certificates for
Python are the Chrome Root Store list in native/lumtub_core/roots.

The yt-dlp zip app in the Android APK is a stable release of yt-dlp (the
Unlicense, public domain), checked against its published SHA2-256SUMS.
QuickJS for YouTube's JavaScript challenges runs inside Lumtub's core (the
rquickjs crate with QuickJS, MIT License); no separate QuickJS program is
included.
